WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.377
This example combines ideas from Modules 11 and 12.

00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:08.587
The standard view owns the stable patient admission logic.

00:00:08.587 --> 00:00:13.527
A common table expression then adds report specific sequence logic.

00:00:13.527 --> 00:00:20.177
The lag function, which gives us the previous value, retrieves the earlier discharge time.

00:00:20.177 --> 00:00:24.846
The report then checks whether the next admission happened within thirty days.

00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:30.100
This is good modular design because stable shared meaning stays in the view,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.454
while a temporary analytical rule stays in the report.
